Subject: [PATCH] msm_vidc_enc: the old spelling of VEN_MSG_FLUSH_OUTPUT_DONE

The video encoder HAL this platform's ROM builds (hardware/qcom-caf/msm8952,
libOmxVenc) was written against the kernel headers of its time, where the
message was spelled VEN_MSG_FLUSH_OUPUT_DONE; this header corrected it. Both
names, the same value.
---
--- include/uapi/linux/msm_vidc_enc.h
+++ include/uapi/linux/msm_vidc_enc.h
@@ -39,6 +39,8 @@
 #define VEN_MSG_NEED_OUTPUT_BUFFER	3
 #define VEN_MSG_FLUSH_INPUT_DONE	4
 #define VEN_MSG_FLUSH_OUTPUT_DONE	5
+/* As older headers spelled it, and older userspace still does. */
+#define VEN_MSG_FLUSH_OUPUT_DONE	VEN_MSG_FLUSH_OUTPUT_DONE
 #define VEN_MSG_START	6
 #define VEN_MSG_STOP	7
 #define VEN_MSG_PAUSE	8
